WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.720
On-screen relationships aren’t always the same&nbsp;
off-screen. In fact, some actors said no to a role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:12.640
just because of a grudge. So, who has bad blood?&nbsp;
Maybe Dom and Hobbs? Keep watching to find out.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.440
From the "X-Men" to "The Lord of&nbsp;
the Rings," Ian McKellen has done it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.480
all in show business. His&nbsp;
versatile filmography and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:25.840
endless list of accolades offer a dizzying&nbsp;
array of reasons why he's considered one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:31.840
the greatest thespians of our time. McKellen&nbsp;
doesn't ask for roles — the roles come to him.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:37.120
"You shall not pass!"

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:42.720
Yet there is one iconic part he declined based&nbsp;
purely on a comment made by a fellow British&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:48.800
actor. As McKellen recalled in a BBC HARDtalk&nbsp;
interview, the late Richard Harris lumped McKellen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:54.240
in the same category as Kenneth Branagh [BRA-nuh]&nbsp;
and Derek Jacobi. What is that category, you ask?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.720
Not a very nice one, despite those actors'&nbsp;
prominence: Harris referred to them as,

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.440
"Technically brilliant, but passionless [actors]."

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.000
Ouch! When Harris passed away, the&nbsp;
"Harry Potter" producers reached out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.120
to McKellen to take over the&nbsp;
role of Professor Dumbledore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:14.080
However, McKellen couldn't quite forget&nbsp;
Harris' opinion of him. McKellen revealed,

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.400
"When they called me up and said, would I be&nbsp;
interested in being in the 'Harry Potter' films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:22.320
they didn't say what part. I worked&nbsp;
out what they were thinking ... and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:27.200
I couldn't. I couldn't take over the part from&nbsp;
an actor who I'd known didn't approve of me."

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.680
Cheekily, he added that he&nbsp;
still played the, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:33.680
"real wizard," referring to Gandalf of&nbsp;
"The Lord of the Rings." Ultimately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.920
Michael Gambon ended up replacing Harris&nbsp;
as Dumbledore for the rest of the films.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:44.080
Bill Murray is a true original. From the fact&nbsp;
that he refuses to have a manager or agent field&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:49.040
his scripts to his overall detachment from the&nbsp;
movie biz, he dances to the beat of his own drum.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.800
However, Murray's laid-back demeanor&nbsp;
hasn't stopped him from being labeled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.920
"The Murricane" by Dan Aykroyd or feuding&nbsp;
with other talents. That latter trait has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:03.200
even resulted in a rift between Murray and a&nbsp;
collaborator he used to call a close friend.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:08.000
Harold Ramis and Murray were practically joined&nbsp;
at the hip for most of the '70s and '80s:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.040
They teamed up on everything from&nbsp;
"Caddyshack" to "Ghostbusters."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:15.360
But during the filming of "Groundhog Day,"&nbsp;
their relationship took a turn for the worse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.120
The two men disagreed about the tone of&nbsp;
the film: Murray wanted something more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:24.160
existential while Ramis was looking for&nbsp;
pure comedy. Their argument grew so heated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:28.160
they refused to speak to each other and&nbsp;
only communicated through assistants.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.280
"Don’t mess with me pork chop."

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.560
Unfortunately, this disagreement caused a rift&nbsp;
that lasted for years. Efforts were made to bridge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:41.600
the gap with variable results: Ramis extended&nbsp;
an olive branch by offering Murray a role in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:46.880
2005's "The Ice Harvest," but he declined.&nbsp;
Respect remained between the two talents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:52.800
however — Ramis praised Murray's work in 2009 and&nbsp;
expressed gratitude for what they'd done together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:58.320
Fortunately, the two old friends reconciled&nbsp;
in 2014, shortly before Ramis passed away.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.400
When one looks back at "Batman Forever," it's&nbsp;
almost impossible to believe the production&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:10.080
actually happened considering all the beef on set.&nbsp;
Joel Schumacher told Entertainment Weekly that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.800
he'd heard horror stories about Val but decided&nbsp;
to hire him anyway. This sort of decision had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.440
worked out for him in the past, after all.&nbsp;
But Kilmer was different. Schumacher said,

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:24.400
"[They] had a physical pushing match. He was&nbsp;
being irrational and ballistic with the first AD,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:29.120
the cameraman, the costume people. He was&nbsp;
badly behaved, he was rude and inappropriate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:33.360
I was forced to tell him that this would&nbsp;
not be tolerated for one more second.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.960
Then we had two weeks where he did&nbsp;
not speak to me, but it was bliss."

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:41.200
In Kilmer's memoir, "Val Kilmer: I'm&nbsp;
Your Huckleberry," the actor reveals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.120
he struggled to act because of the&nbsp;
confining and heavy Batsuit. This,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:49.680
he claims, led to the tension between him&nbsp;
and Schumacher. As a result, he decided not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:54.880
to return for "Batman and Robin." Schumacher,&nbsp;
though, sees things differently. As he told EW,

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.920
"He sort of quit, we sort of fired him. It&nbsp;
probably depends on who's telling the story."

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:06.240
Regardless, one truth emerges: George Clooney&nbsp;
became the one bearing the burden of the Batsuit.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:12.080
When a film pulls off a character named&nbsp;
Dirk Diggler, it deserves all the accolades&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:17.440
possible — and a heaping helping of "shut up&nbsp;
and take my money" memes to boot. Fortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:22.960
Paul Thomas Anderson's 1997 classic,&nbsp;
"Boogie Nights," received all that and more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:27.600
including a best supporting actor nomination&nbsp;
for Burt Reynolds, who portrayed Jack Horner.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:33.280
Despite positive reception from both critics and&nbsp;
audiences, Reynolds wasn't a fan of the film or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.760
the director. According to The Guardian,&nbsp;
he admitted that he'd never even watched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:42.880
the entire movie. He told GQ that he didn't&nbsp;
want to work with Anderson ever again, adding,

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:48.720
"Personality-wise, we didn't fit. I think mostly&nbsp;
because he was young and full of himself. Every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:53.200
shot we did, it was like the first time [that&nbsp;
shot had ever been done]. I remember the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:57.680
shot we did in 'Boogie Nights,' where I drive the&nbsp;
car to Grauman's Theater. After he said, 'Isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:02.640
that amazing?' And I named five pictures that&nbsp;
had the same kind of shot. It wasn't original."

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:08.000
Anderson tried to mend fences by offering Reynolds&nbsp;
a role in his next project, "Magnolia," but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:13.760
the storied actor turned it down. He told The&nbsp;
Guardian that he hated Anderson, before adding,

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:17.520
"I'd done my picture with Paul Thomas&nbsp;
Anderson, that was enough for me."

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:23.440
While "Sex and the City" is all about the&nbsp;
unbreakable bond between four New York women,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:27.120
making it wasn't quite a stroll&nbsp;
through Central Park. In particular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.320
stars Kim Cattrall [kuh-TRAHL],&nbsp;
who played bold Samantha Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:35.760
and Sarah Jessica Parker, who played open-hearted&nbsp;
Carrie Bradshaw, had some major differences.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:41.360
For years, there were rumblings that the two&nbsp;
actors didn't get along. But for just as long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.600
they seemed to be able to put their personal&nbsp;
feelings aside for the sake of the show and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:51.200
two subsequent movies. In 2017, however,&nbsp;
tensions escalated to new heights after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:56.480
Cattrall failed to sign on for the proposed&nbsp;
"Sex and the City 3." Not long after this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:02.320
her brother passed away and Parker reached out to&nbsp;
offer her condolences. Cattrall didn't appreciate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:06.800
this gesture. She took to her Instagram&nbsp;
account where she addressed Parker directly:

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:11.040
"Your continuous reaching out is&nbsp;
a painful reminder of how cruel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:16.240
you really were then and now. Let me make&nbsp;
this VERY clear. (If I haven't already)&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:20.560
You are not my family. You are not my&nbsp;
friend. So I'm writing to tell you one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:26.320
last time to stop exploiting our tragedy in&nbsp;
order to restore your 'nice girl' persona."

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:30.400
Unsurprisingly, Cattrall&nbsp;
decided not to join the 2021&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:34.560
HBO Max "Sex and the City" revival&nbsp;
series, "And Just Like That."

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.280
Imagine this for a second:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:42.080
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson and Vin Diesel&nbsp;
having a heated disagreement on set.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:46.880
Can't you practically smell all the testosterone&nbsp;
in the air? Perhaps this didn't help matters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:53.120
as Johnson possibly blasted his co-star in a&nbsp;
now-deleted 2016 post to his Instagram account.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:59.280
He didn't name names, but his feelings were clear:&nbsp;
Of his male "Fast and Furious" co-stars, he said,

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.960
"Some conduct themselves as stand&nbsp;
up men and true professionals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:05.520
while others don't ... Candy a--es."

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:11.680
While the actors were quick to downplay the feud,&nbsp;
a 2021 Vanity Fair interview with Johnson revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:17.040
the full extent of it. Turns out, Johnson only&nbsp;
returned for "The Fate of the Furious" under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:21.920
the strict rule that he and Diesel not&nbsp;
share any scenes together. Johnson said,

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:26.720
"I wanted to forgo drama. I thought that that&nbsp;
was the best thing to do. For everybody."

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:31.120
Since then, the two have taken subtle&nbsp;
digs at one another in a variety of ways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:36.080
leading many to speculate that Johnson's absence&nbsp;
from "F9" was due to the continued hostility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:41.120
between him and Diesel. There's no irrefutable&nbsp;
confirmation that this was the case, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:44.160
and the stars have gone out of their&nbsp;
way to show each other respect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:49.280
Does that mean the feud is over? No one knows.&nbsp;
The future could hold anything for these two and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:54.720
the franchise they share — especially if The Rock&nbsp;
decides it's octane that he wants to be cookin'.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:58.960
The real reason behind Charlie&nbsp;
Sheen's exit from "Two and a Half&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:03.360
Men" is one of the most complicated&nbsp;
entertainment stories of the 2010s.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:08.160
In 2011, the show went on a hiatus in an&nbsp;
effort to help the actor deal with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:13.120
personal problems. However, Sheen refused&nbsp;
to enter a rehab facility and proceeded to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:18.080
start a bizarre public fight with showrunner&nbsp;
Chuck Lorre. Eventually, the actor was fired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:23.200
from the sitcom. He responded by penning a&nbsp;
letter that was published on TMZ. He wrote,

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:26.480
"I wish [Lorre] nothing but&nbsp;
pain in his silly travels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:30.800
especially if they wind up in my octagon.&nbsp;
Clearly I have defeated this earthworm with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:34.560
my words — imagine what I would have&nbsp;
done with my fire breathing fists."

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:39.520
"Two and a Half Men" continued without Sheen.&nbsp;
However, the producers offered him an opportunity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:44.480
to return for the series finale. As Lorre&nbsp;
explained, Sheen declined because he wanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:49.040
the ending to spin off into another sitcom&nbsp;
called "The Harpers." According to Yahoo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:52.880
in the years since the incident, Sheen has&nbsp;
admitted that he could've handled the whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:57.520
situation better. Maybe the grudge between&nbsp;
him and Lorre is well and truly over now.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:03.280
The show might've been called "Charmed," but it&nbsp;
probably should've been named "Cursed," judging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:09.520
by all the drama that happened on set. For Shannen&nbsp;
Doherty and Alyssa Milano, their beef got so bad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:14.560
the former decided she'd had enough and&nbsp;
left the show altogether after Season 3.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:17.920
Chatting about her decision to&nbsp;
Entertainment Tonight, Doherty said,

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:21.920
"There was too much drama on the set and&nbsp;
not enough passion for the work. You know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:26.160
I'm 30 years old and I don't have time for&nbsp;
drama in my life anymore [...] [I want]&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:30.960
to work with actors who really, really care&nbsp;
and that want to be there every single day."

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:36.320
Yikes! Years later, Milano and Doherty&nbsp;
reconnected and repaired their relationship.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:42.480
Speaking on E!'s Daily Pop in 2017, Milano&nbsp;
said that they made amends via Twitter DMs.

